/*  The project of Cufet written in Cufet — and the first to draw its tree.

    ★★ `front-end` is ONE namespace spread over three folders. The lexer, the parser and the
    checker share their types and helpers — `node`, `token`, `field-of` — by their plain names, so a
    wall between them would mean qualifying nearly every line. The drawing folds the three folders
    into `front-end`: organised apart, named together.

    ⚠ Once a project draws its tree it draws every folder with Cufet source in it. A new folder
    here needs a line before anything in it can be checked.
*/

Pull a book on blueprints.
    Bind text to tree:
        Return <<
front-end
    lexer
    parser
    checker
>>.
    Done.
Done.
